Z||000000||FieroJoe||03-22-2001||10:44 PM||||I was looking through your photopoint album, and thought that those daytime running lamps were pretty cool.  A few questions about them:<P>Are they just the front turn signal bulbs that are always on when the ignition is on?<P>Did you wire it yourself or buy a kit (i know of at least one that is available to buy)<P>anything else special about them?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-23-2001||01:24 PM||||They are the stock blinker bulbs. It is hooked so that when the car is started they light the bright bulb elements.(What was the blinker element.)If the blinker or 4 ways go on, the lights will shut and the dim lights turn on. this makes the blinking action. If the car is off and the 4 ways are turned on, the dim lights blink.<P>Let me try to explain how I hooked them up.<BR><B>SEE PICS</B><P>1. I spliced a wire to the Ignition on wire under the dash so it would be hot when the car is on. (SEE YELLOW WIRE)<P>2. I got an automotive relay. I hooked the yellow wire to the relay as shown.<P>3. I cut the harness near the light bulb.<P>4. I hooked the blue wire from the bulb harness to the relay so that when the relay is sitting with no power going to anything but the yellow wire it would give power to the blue bulb wire.<P>5. I hooked the relay ground up<P>6. I took the Brown bulb wire and spliced it with the Blue wire coming from the harness. It was then hooked to the relays secondary so it would activate the relay when power was in the blue wire. (it would light the dim bulb element.<P>7.Tuck Yellow wire under weather strip<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DTRL.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dt2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dt3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dt4.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||03-23-2001||01:26 PM||||I hope I helped. I don't know if I explained it good or not.||||reg||10
Z||000003||shiloh187||03-23-2001||05:54 PM||||on the 88, where did you get the white gauge faces, they are the nicest i have seen so far.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||03-23-2001||06:03 PM||||Perfect explanation!  I will be doing that soon I think.  Very clever way of doing it, I understand it totally.<P>I had a bunch of bosch type relays (7), but I used all of them in my alarm install.  I'll have to wait until I find a bunch more stuff to order from <A HREF="http://www.partsexpress.com" TARGET=_blank>www.partsexpress.com</A>  because they are only $.99 ea ($5 ea at radio shack), but if you dont order enough they really ding ya on shipping.  I had an that totaled about $3 in resistors, and they charged me $7.36 to ship it.  When I ordered my alarm system and all the relays and some other electronics parts, (total over $100), shipping was only $3.  Crazy.<P>But yeah, I'll definatly be doing that mod if you dont mind!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||TheFiero64||03-23-2001||07:53 PM||||shiloh187, Thanks for the complement. I got them from <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm</A>  They do not include the warning light overlays. I made those myself. I was selling a batch, but I ran out. I may make some more soon. I will let you know when I do.<P><B>FieroJoe</B>I am glad you could understand me. I love my lights. It looks like all the new cars. They are nice and bright.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||03-23-2001||10:12 PM||||I have the same white face gauge overlays!  Got them off of ebay, and the guy sent me a second set for no reason!<P>If you ever get around to making the warning light overlays again, I would definatly be interested in a set.  <P>One more question about the lights.  Do you have a relay for both sides, or just the one to control both of them?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000007||TheFiero64||03-24-2001||10:12 AM||||There is one for each side. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
